# ocr_handler
#
# This project downloads MODEL WEIGHTS. Nothing downloaded, generated, or
# rendered belongs in git. Source and docs only.

# --- Virtual environment --------------------------------------------------
# 271 MB with pymupdf/numpy/scipy; will exceed 3 GB once torch and a model
# land. Rebuilt by `uv sync` from the committed uv.lock.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Model weights and caches ---------------------------------------------
# UniMERNet-Base is ~1.3 GB, SmolDocling ~500 MB, Unlimited-OCR 6.2 GB bf16 /
# 2.6 GB NF4. A single accidental commit of any of these is unrecoverable
# without rewriting history.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.bin
!**/site-packages/**          # (unreachable — .venv/ already ignored; kept as intent)

models/
weights/
checkpoints/
.cache/
huggingface/
hf_cache/
torch_cache/
*.nf4/                        # locally quantised model dumps

# --- Generated output -----------------------------------------------------
# tmp/ is the scratch output directory. Renders, crops, masks, extracted ink.
# All reproducible from the source PDFs.
tmp/
out/
output/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# --- Tooling caches -------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editors / OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ---------------------------------------------
# uv.lock        -> commit; it is what makes the environment reproducible
# pyproject.toml -> commit
# docs/          -> commit; the research is the most valuable artifact here
# src/, tests/   -> commit

# Test fixtures. Operator's call, 2026-09-06.
#
# ⚠ WHAT IS IN HERE IS NOT REGENERABLE BY RUNNING ANYTHING. ground_truth/ holds 236 rows of
# HAND-LABELLED pages -- labels.csv (161) and shred_sweep_labels.csv (75) -- produced by reading
# rendered pages one at a time. They are the evidence behind the shipped precision/recall numbers
# (strict precision 93.1%, recall 68.2%; see docs/findings/recall-was-a-symbol-test-not-a-run-length.md).
# 120 KB, all text, no binaries.
#
# Being ignored means `git clean -fdx` deletes them permanently. To keep a copy under version
# control without un-ignoring the folder:  git add -f tests/fixtures/ground_truth/*.csv
tests/fixtures/
